$ factory worker -h
exit 0
--- stdout
usage: factory worker [flags]

Run the step executor: register with the factory server, claim steps one at a
time, run each, and report the result. Exits 0 when the server has nothing
left to hand out. On SIGTERM the step in hand is released, which counts no
attempt.

Flags (each also read from FACTORY_<FLAG>, e.g. FACTORY_GIT_URL):
  --git-url URL
      base URL of clone URLs, <git-url>/<owner>/<repo>.git (default
      https://github.com)
  --github-api-url URL
      GitHub REST API base URL (default https://api.github.com)
  --harnesses STRING
      agent CLIs to use, in order; those not installed or not logged in are
      skipped (default claude-code,grok)
  --sandbox NAME
      the worker's name, the sandbox it runs in (default: the host name)
  --sandbox-key STRING
      claim only this chain's steps (<item id>/<owner>/<repo>)
  --token-file FILE
      file holding the pod's projected ServiceAccount token, sent once to
      register; the server answers with the worker's credential
  --url URL
      the factory server URL (required)
  --work-dir DIRECTORY
      directory where checkouts live (default $TMPDIR/factory-worker)

Environment:
  FACTORY_API_TOKEN    bearer token when --token-file is not set: for a worker
                       outside Kubernetes, against a server without --launcher
--- stderr
